      },
      "title": "The master server, unused",
      "description": "**What it is:** one server that mounts all nine network servers under prefixes, plus three hand-written tools.\n\n**How it works:** only `backend/run_mcp.py` starts it. It's for testing the tools by hand in an MCP client, like Claude Desktop.\n\n**Why it matters:** your README describes this as *the* tool server, but the agent starts the network servers directly (step 8).\n\n**Watch out:** its three curated tools are placeholders. `full_unity_admob_integration` returns *success* without doing anything. Know this before anyone asks about it."
    },
    {
      "title": "What you can do now",
      "description": "### What you can do now\n\n- Explain MCP in one sentence, and how a Discovery or OpenAPI file becomes tools.\n- Describe how a tool server starts: subprocess, stdio, token in the environment.\n- Explain the two caches and what they save.\n- Say honestly which networks fully work, and why.\n\n**Next:** *11 - The approval pause*. What happens when a tool wants to change your account."
    }
